1. find middle of link list in one pass (just one loop)
   we don't the size of the linked-list!

Note: even linked list has tow middle
      odd linked list has one middle

solution: use two extra pointer as firstMiddle & secondMiddle
          find them on each step!




2. find out if the linked-list has loop or not?
   loop on linked list means we have a node that has a pointer      N1 -> N2 -> N3 -> N4
   to some previous nodes!                                                 ^          |
                                                                           |__________|

Note: in this situation we have not the "LAST" node!
      all the node has NEXT!

solution: use two extra pointer as slow and fast
          slow travel the list by 1X
          fast travel the list by 2X
          if we have loop on linked list, they will see each other!
          (if fast get null, we terminate the function!)

Note: if we have the 1X
      there is not any black hole!
      they have to see each other.
      This algorithm is called "Floyd’s Cycle-finding" Algorithm.